    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Expion360’s core lithium-ion battery storage business is contending with softening OEM demand, which weighed on sales and kept the top line in contraction. While gross margin managed a modest sequential improvement, the broader demand environment remained subdued, reflecting pullback in key downstream applications. Against this backdrop, the company is positioning for a rekindling of momentum through an imminent launch of next-generation products, aiming to broaden its addressable market and re-stimulate order flow.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is leaning into a product-led revival, banking on upcoming advanced storage solutions to unlock new market segments and offset current weakness. The strategic push has been accompanied by a striking shift in market posture: short interest collapsed by half in May, signaling that bearish conviction is unwinding even as the stock suffered a sharp post-earnings selloff. While credibility still awaits a fundamental inflection, the retreat of short bets suggests a slice of the market is cautiously pricing in the possibility that the new product cycle can engineer a turnaround.",
